  "summary": "Real batch-1 decode step is 7-10% faster than AIS at every context (13.75 vs 15.03 ms at ISL 256; 19.4 vs 21.5 ms at 129K). Real idle TTFT is 5-10% slower than AIS prefill from 4K up (2771.9 vs 2550.4 ms at 32K; 22114 vs 20100 ms at 129K), plus about 17 ms of fixed HTTP/frontend/client overhead visible at small ISL (39 vs 22 ms at 256). Net E2E at OSL 256: live/AIS 0.91-0.93 up to 8K, 0.96-0.98 at 16-32K, 1.02-1.07 at 64-129K. Repeatable within 2.2% across two nodes and three runs."
