   "what": "serve-phase frontend never ran: job_node.sh killed the wrapper subshell of a backgrounded step function, so the check frontend kept serving and the serve frontend failed to bind port 18000; readiness was answered by the old frontend",
   "effect_on_this_run": "the cell was served by the check-phase frontend of the same plan and policy (policy_evidence ok on it); its router had served 26 probe requests and the workers were flushed and proven cold before the payload, so the payload saw identical config and empty caches but not a fresh router process (policy RNG draws and the indexer's probe entries carried over); hypothesis: no measurable effect, since probe blocks never overlap workload blocks",
   "fix": "<commit-37>: background srun launched directly (PID is srun), wait for the port to close, require the new frontend alive after readiness, bounded teardown",
   "verified": "job <job-4>: four fresh frontends (check and serve for default_defaults and round_robin), each logged shutdown, no port conflicts, round_robin serve config router_mode round-robin, policy switch took 27 s"
